I've completed the semantic-hint injection for this WebTestBench app (a "TechSpecs KB" documentation/knowledge-base SPA with three view tabs: Documents, Knowledge Graph, and Favorites, plus a 404 page).

## What I did

1. Read the spec (`hint-design.md`) first, as required.
2. Explored the app: `src/pages/Index.tsx` (tab shell), `DocumentList`, `DocumentViewer`, `DocumentSection`, `KnowledgeGraph`, `Toast`, `EmptyState`, `ModuleBadge`, `FavoriteButton`, `NotFound`.
3. Widened three shared presentational components (`ModuleBadge`, `FavoriteButton`, `EmptyState`) with `ComponentProps<'span'|'button'|'div'>` + `{...props}` spread — the one code change the spec permits — so call sites can pass distinct `data-semtag-*` ids.
4. Injected hints across every screen: header tab navigation, the Documents/Favorites master-detail views (search, module-filter toggles, sort select, document collection, favorite toggle), section expand/collapse + in-section link collections, the document viewer (back nav, module/favorite/date/version/title/description observables, related-docs collection), the Knowledge Graph (zoom controls, zoom-level observable, node collection), the toast notification, and the 404 page's return-home link.

## Validation

- `node .../validate-semtags.mjs src` → **38 hinted elements, 0 errors, 0 warnings**.
- `npx tsc --noEmit` → clean.
- `npm run lint` → same 3 pre-existing errors/8 warnings as before my changes, all in files I never touched (`ui/command.tsx`, `ui/textarea.tsx`, `tailwind.config.ts`, plus a pre-existing `useMemo` dep warning in `DocumentList.tsx` on a line I didn't modify).
- `npm run build` → succeeds.
- Manually confirmed every `role="collection"` container is a real DOM ancestor of its items, and that all template-literal ids (doc ids, section ids, module keys, graph node ids) are stable domain keys, unique at runtime.

## Id namespaces introduced

`nav.tab.*`, `documents.sidebar/list/filters/search/sort/filter.module.*/item.*`, `favorites.sidebar/list/...` (same shape, scoped separately), `document.viewer.*` (back, module, favorite, updated, version, title, description, related.item.*), `<docId>.section.<sectionId>` (+`.links.item.<targetDocId>`), `graph.panel/zoomIn/zoomOut/reset/zoomLevel/nodes.item.<docId>`, `app.toast(.dismiss)`, `notfound.home`.

## Left unhinted (deliberate)

- The graph legend (static, decorative, duplicates node colors already visible in the graph).
- `ModuleBadge` inside document-list rows and related-doc cards — kept only on the viewer header, to avoid duplicating the same category label on every row for token economy (agents can already filter by module via the toggle group).
- Section body text and "Content Sections"/"Related Documents" headings — static copy, not state to act on or read.

No collections failed to fold — all four repeated structures (document list/favorites list, per-section links, related-docs grid, graph nodes) satisfy the container+`.item.<key>` rule with ≥2 items and real domain keys.

